{"skill":{"slug":"pdf","displayName":"Pdf"},"version":{"version":"0.1.0","createdAt":1769847855729,"changelog":"- Initial release of the PDF manipulation toolkit.\n- Supports text and table extraction, PDF creation, merging, splitting, metadata extraction, and rotation.\n- Guides for handling scanned PDFs (OCR), password protection, watermarking, and image extraction.\n- Provides command-line tool usage (pdftotext, qpdf, pdftk, pdfimages).\n- Recipes and code examples for Python libraries: pypdf, pdfplumber, and reportlab.\n- Quick reference and next steps included for users needing advanced or form-related workflows.","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":7068,"sha256":"38d8559d4899602f82f3560052132aa0c40cfca80203037729756bdb4fb8e0cb","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2018,"sha256":"de8931a4cf717dbe2c7bfbb7f429dfc3aa18bfa4d9fdbf686b1a125f0dff227c","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789024297762,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"4991fa905d1b4d6d2995d44812f6859297d385965b4078be001c2bfd0908017c","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/4991fa905d1b4d6d2995d44812f6859297d385965b4078be001c2bfd0908017c","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: pdf\nVersion: 0.1.0\n\nThe skill bundle, primarily through `SKILL.md`, provides extensive examples for PDF manipulation using both Python libraries and command-line tools such as `pdftotext`, `qpdf`, `pdftk`, and `pdfimages`. The inclusion of command-line tool examples implies the agent will have shell access and perform file system interactions, which are high-risk capabilities. Although these actions are directly aligned with the stated purpose of a 'comprehensive PDF manipulation toolkit,' the inherent risk associated with shell access without clear sandboxing or restrictions warrants a 'suspicious' classification. There is no evidence of intentional malicious behavior, data exfiltration, or prompt injection attempts to subvert the agent's purpose.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779160401037},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":18,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":2,"checkedAt":1789024297762},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a straightforward PDF-processing guide with some sensitive-capable examples, but no hidden behavior, persistence, exfiltration, or automatic execution.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The skill operates on user-specified PDF files using common local Python libraries and PDF command-line tools, which is proportionate for the stated purpose.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"There is no automatic installer or bundled executable code; one OCR example suggests installing pytesseract and pdf2image without pinned versions or hashes.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The instructions are ordinary PDF workflow examples and do not attempt to override agent behavior; the qpdf password-removal example is purpose-aligned but would benefit from an explicit authorization warning for protected documents.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No persistence, background workers, privilege escalation, credential collection, session use, or network retrieval/execution behavior was found in the artifact.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The documented capabilities match the stated PDF purpose: reading, extracting text and tables, creating, merging, splitting, rotating, OCR, watermarking, image extraction, form handling references, and password protection/removal.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install this skill only if you want local PDF-processing guidance. Use password-removal commands only for PDFs you own or are explicitly authorized to access, and install optional Python packages in a virtual environment from trusted sources, ideally with pinned versions.","findings":"[SDI-2] expected: The artifact does include a qpdf decrypt example for removing a password from an encrypted PDF; because it requires a supplied password and fits PDF manipulation, this is not enough to make the skill suspicious, though users should only use it on documents they own or are authorized to process.\n[SQP-2] expected: The protected-PDF handling concern is valid as safety guidance: the skill lacks an authorization caveat, but the behavior is disclosed, narrow, and not hidden or automatic.\n[T08] expected: The OCR example mentions installing pytesseract and pdf2image without version pins; this is common documentation-style dependency guidance rather than an install script, so it remains a dependency hygiene note rather than a material security concern.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789024297762}}}}}